SupraLINUX Thunderbolt integration

Keep official sources unchanged, all three upstream tests, the KDED module,
the private libkbolt implementation, the KCM QML UI and Ubuntu runtime Bolt.
Do not expose a new public SDK or silently remove the configuration module.
Tests load the actual installed modules. Unmodified upstream fake Bolt providers
serve only org.kde.fakebolt on a dedicated session bus using KBOLT_FAKE=1;
the real system bus and hardware are never used by this package fixture.
Check actual notifications, both authorization actions, flags, enrollment,
authorized-device suppression, real KCM QML rendering, enabled device labels and
dynamic device removal. Ubuntu may emit transient QML diagnostics during removal;
keep the original stdout/stderr for comparison with the candidate and desktop QA.
Compile the baseline client against Ubuntu Qt/Frameworks, preserve its bytes
across the candidate upgrade, then compile and run a new consumer. Private HOME,
XDG state, offscreen Qt, software rendering and bounded sessions are required.
These checks certify package integration with the simulated Bolt protocol;
physical Thunderbolt hardware and a complete Wayland desktop remain later QA.
